# `use` switches exhaustively over dep's sealed interface S (permits X, Y), with no default.
# Adding Z to the permits list changes no member of S, only its PermittedSubclasses attribute, yet
# makes the switch non-exhaustive. The change must reach S's API hash, or `use` is not recompiled
# and the build stays green when it should fail. Cross-module, so the external-API path is checked.
> use/compile
$ sleep 2000
$ copy-file changes/S.java dep/src/main/java/S.java
$ copy-file changes/Z.java dep/src/main/java/Z.java
-> use/compile
> use/clean
> dep/clean
-> use/compile
